{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"b2b4a5c6f08218f8877599788e7d2e950dcffb4bcfbde356cb6a70b8a3c86b30","packTokens":1209,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":206,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":428,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":469,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Keep the data in the project's PostgreSQL database (the connection string named App, which the project already reads).\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Write its sample data in App.Api/SeedData.cs: a few believable rows for each table, taken from the contract's examples, so each list has something to show.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"The app runs that file only when the setting Seed:Demo is true, so no test may count on those rows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"The web app is built in its own repo; do not build screens here.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Which API data must be persisted in PostgreSQL?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Persist all application data that API operations read or change, including values derived or cached for later requests.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"When the application adds its data model to the existing PostgreSQL database, what should happen to any pre-existing database contents?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Preserve existing contents and add the application structures without discarding compatible data.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"When a ration defines ingredient proportions, what basis should the API use to calculate inventory consumption and ration cost?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Treat proportions as percentages of as-fed ingredient weight; use dry-matter values only for nutritional calculations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen when recording a feeding event whose ration requires more of an ingredient than is currently in inventory?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Reject the entire event without changing inventory or feed rollups.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the feed-to-gain metrics and projected ship date be represented when Days on Feed is zero or ADG is zero or negative?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Return the affected metrics and projected ship date as unavailable until the required positive denominator or gain exists.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement every HTTP operation in the OpenAPI contract with its declared methods, paths, parameters, schemas, security, statuses, and behavior.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Persist application values, including derived and cached values, in PostgreSQL through the existing App connection string; make committed values available to later requests and after restart; and initialize required structures without deleting or changing compatible existing data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is true on a clean database, run SeedData.Run at startup to populate each application table with two or three believable sample rows based on contract examples.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is false, do not run SeedData.Run or insert demo rows at startup, and serve contract operations without requiring demo rows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Keep the repository a backend API and documentation surface, without product-facing web screens or frontend implementation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Calculate ingredient consumption and ration cost from as-fed ingredient weights, using dry-matter values only for nutritional calculations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Reject a feeding event with status 409, without changing inventory or feed rollups, when any required ration ingredient exceeds available inventory.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Return ADG as null when Days on Feed is zero; return feedConversionRatio and costOfGain as null when a weight-gain denominator is nonpositive; and return projectedShipDate as null when ADG is nonpositive or no positive gain remains toward the target.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}